<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aboud Jumbe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1920–2016</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Aboud Jumbe Mwinyi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aboud Jumbe was a Zanzibari politician who became president of Zanzibar and first vice-president of Tanzania after the assassination of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abeid-karume">Abeid Karume</a> in 1972. He took the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afro-shirazi-party">Afro-Shirazi Party</a> into the merger with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanganyika-african-national-union">TANU</a> that created <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chama-cha-mapinduzi">Chama Cha Mapinduzi</a> in 1977 and introduced a separate Zanzibar constitution in 1979. He was forced to resign in 1984 amid accusations that he sought greater autonomy for the islands.</p></div>
